{"stage": "step:s2", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2628, "output_tokens": 606, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "I read the six remaining project documents and recorded the results. The key finding is that Module-D2 should be ruled out, even though it gives the highest light collection.\n\n**Robustness constraint (thermal_cycling_tests.md):** Requirement is at most 5% failures after 20 cycles between 300 K and 87 K.\n- Module-D2: 30% failed (the thin light-guide bonding cracks on cooldown). This fails the requirement by a wide margin.\n- Module-D3: 2% failed. Passes.\n- Module-D1: 0.5% failed. Passes.\n\nSince modules cannot be accessed after the cryostat is filled, D2 is ruled out despite its 38 PE/MeV at 20% coverage in the 2025 simulation.\n\n**Other documents:**\n- **Cryostat.md:** Argon purity better than 100 ppt O2-equivalent is expected. No design constraint.\n- **Electronics.md:** Cold amplifiers are validated for every candidate design. No design constraint.\n- **Meeting notes (2026-01-20):** Feedthroughs support up to 30% coverage. The full allowed coverage range is available.\n- **Schedule.md:** Design freeze in Q3, production next year. No design constraint.\n- **Simulation summary (2025):** At 20% coverage, D2 gave 38 PE/MeV, D3 27, and D1 18. Light collection scales roughly as coverage^0.8. These numbers are from an earlier study and predate the thermal-cycling result, so they do not account for D2's robustness failure.\n\n**Implication for later steps:** The remaining choice is between Module-D3 (higher light yield, 2% failure) and Module-D1 (lower yield, 0.5% failure). Both pass the robustness requirement. Coverage can be anywhere from 5% to 30%.", "type": "text"}]}
