{"stage": "step:s3", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4751, "output_tokens": 457, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "I ran the light-collection simulation for all three designs at six wall coverages (5% to 30%, 18 runs total) and recorded the results.\n\n| Coverage | D1 (PE/MeV) | D2 (PE/MeV) | D3 (PE/MeV) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5% | 5.90 | 12.35 | 9.32 |\n| 10% | 10.75 | 21.67 | 15.58 |\n| 15% | 15.09 | 30.05 | 22.11 |\n| 20% | 18.66 | 37.25 | 26.96 |\n| 25% | 21.58 | 44.42 | 32.46 |\n| 30% | 24.60 | 50.87 | 38.88 |\n\nD2 gives the highest light collection at every coverage, reaching 50.9 PE/MeV at 30%. D1 is the lowest at every coverage.\n\nThese numbers are light collection only. Earlier results show D2 has a thermal failure fraction of 0.30, against an allowed maximum of 0.05, and it has already been ruled out on robustness grounds. D3 (0.02) and D1 (0.005) both pass. Since modules cannot be serviced after the cryostat is filled, the robustness constraint takes precedence over D2's light-yield advantage. The recommendation will need to come from D1 or D3, and that decision belongs to the next step.", "type": "text"}]}
{"stage": "step:s4", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1695, "output_tokens": 447, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 323}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01TwbiqjzvaZyqjjHB1x5E2b", "input": {"results": {"selected_design_index": 3, "selected_coverage_pct": 30, "selected_PE_per_MeV": 38.875, "thermal_fail_frac_selected": 0.02, "module_D2_eliminated": 1}}, "name": "record_results", "type": "tool_use", "caller": {"type": "direct"}}]}
{"stage": "step:s4", "tool": "record_results", "input": {"results": {"selected_design_index": 3, "selected_coverage_pct": 30, "selected_PE_per_MeV": 38.875, "thermal_fail_frac_selected": 0.02, "module_D2_eliminated": 1}}, "result": "Recorded."}
{"stage": "step:s4", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2152, "output_tokens": 513, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "Module-D3 at 30% wall coverage is the selected design, giving 38.875 PE/MeV.\n\n**Robustness screen:**\n- **Module-D2 is eliminated.** Its thermal failure fraction is 0.30, well above the 0.05 limit. Its higher yield (for example, 50.873 PE/MeV at 30%) does not offset a 30% thermal failure rate in a module that cannot be accessed after the cryostat is filled.\n- **Module-D1 passes** the thermal criterion (0.005 failure fraction), but its yield is much lower: 24.598 PE/MeV at 30%.\n- **Module-D3 passes** the thermal criterion (0.02 failure fraction).\n\n**Selection:** Among the surviving designs, D3 at 30% gives the highest light collection, 38.875 PE/MeV versus 24.598 for D1 at 30%. The 30% coverage is the maximum allowed and is within the feedthrough support limit of 30%. The electronics were validated for all designs.\n\n**Trade-off:** D3 gives up some yield relative to the eliminated D2 (38.9 vs. 50.9 PE/MeV at 30%), but it keeps the thermal failure fraction at 2%, which is the price of robustness for inaccessible modules.\n\nI recorded the selected design index as 3 (Module-D3, the third listed design), coverage 30%, and the expected yield of 38.875 PE/MeV. The index is 1-based; if a later step expects 0-based indexing, D3 would be index 2.", "type": "text"}]}
{"stage": "step:s5", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1710, "output_tokens": 440, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 385}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013mnvBBxVwMpU9L6pBJgaBX", "input": {"name": "candidate_specs.md"}, "name": "read_document", "type": "tool_use", "caller": {"type": "direct"}}]}
