{"stage": "step:s5", "tool": "record_results", "input": {"results": {"final_design_index": 3, "final_coverage_pct": 30, "final_PE_per_MeV": 38.875, "final_thermal_fail_frac": 0.02, "thermal_fail_max_allowed": 0.05, "D2_PE_per_MeV_30pct_ruled_out": 50.873, "D2_thermal_fail_frac": 0.3}}, "result": "Recorded."}
{"stage": "step:s5", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2484, "output_tokens": 565, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "**Recommendation: Module-D3 (wavelength-shifting bar with SiPM readout) at 30% wall coverage.**\n\n**Light collection**\n- Module-D3 at 30%: 38.875 PE/MeV, the highest among the designs that pass the robustness screen.\n- For comparison, Module-D1 at 30% gives 24.598 PE/MeV, and Module-D2 at 30% gives 50.873 PE/MeV.\n\n**Robustness justification**\n- Modules cannot be accessed once the cryostat is filled, so thermal-cycling failure is the deciding constraint.\n- Module-D2 has a thermal failure fraction of 0.30, far above the 0.05 limit. It has the highest light yield, but it is ruled out on robustness grounds, which is why it is excluded despite its PE/MeV.\n- Module-D3 has a thermal failure fraction of 0.02, which is under the 0.05 limit. It gives roughly 58% more light than Module-D1 at the same coverage.\n- Module-D1 is the most robust (0.005 failure fraction), but its light yield is about 37% lower than D3's at 30% coverage. D3 is the better balance of light yield and reliability.\n- Electronics were validated for all designs, and the feedthroughs support coverage up to 30%, so 30% is within the allowed range.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The thermal failure fractions come from earlier project steps. `candidate_specs.md` itself contains only the design descriptions and no robustness data, so the 0.02 figure for D3 should be confirmed against the underlying test data before commitment.\n- D3 at 30% is at the top of the allowed coverage range, so there is no margin above that.", "type": "text"}]}
